dit/080: ggml-opencl gives the GPU back to the screen. GGML_OPENCL_YIELD_EVERY=N waits for the queue every N ops and
sleeps GGML_OPENCL_YIELD_US; GGML_OPENCL_MM_MAX_GFLOP splits a big matmul into token chunks with a yield between;
GGML_OPENCL_YIELD_LOG=1 prints the longest wait per graph. The S25 lagged severely running Z-Image on OpenCL with
2.2 GB of RAM free: the UI and the DiT share the Adreno, and one FFN matmul at 512^2 was an 80 ms dispatch.
Text before the first diff line is ignored by git apply.

